From 91d141f9a59ee72fc071272e1e043e87a9740943 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bugcheck <bugcheck@local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:50:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pedestrians: walk on real sidewalks, turn corners, wait at
 the kerb

Audit (tools/probe_peds.gd, 2 min x 4 spots): walkers walked / waited / stood on the
carriageway (Orange & 4th: 1327 walk-on-road samples; Amber: 469 waiting in the road,
316 standing still there, up to 33 s).
- Root cause: the junction table _node_all was keyed by float node ids (JSON) while
  every lookup passes an int -> every junction set-back was 0 and _ped_turn found no
  street at any corner (walkers turned back = 'can't decide where to go'). Walkers now
  use an int-keyed copy (_node_all_i / _ped_setback). Cars keep the old table: fixing
  it for cars deadlocks scripted rides (junction booking tuned to it) -> separate task.
- Corners at the cross street's kerb (_corner_s = set-back - 1.5 m), not 4 m from the node.
- Street pieces with < 4 m of sidewalk outside their junctions are not walked.
- A sidewalk side inside another carriageway (inner side of a dual carriageway) is never
  used (_ped_side_ok); corner turns that cut across a road > 7 m wide are rejected
  (_ped_walk_crosses_road), alley / driveway mouths are walked across.
After: walking on the road 1327/485/235/138 -> 1/19/0/4; waiting in the road 469/126 -> 0;
standing still on the road 316/57 -> 0. test_traffic, cityride, taxi, hitchhike,
scripted, positions pass (before the side / turn-cut additions; re-run pending).
---
 traffic/traffic_sim.gd | 123 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 93 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

